Emerging Market Opportunities
Digital health and connected inhalers
Connected inhalers and mobile health platforms offer opportunities to monitor medication use and support patient education. These tools may help healthcare professionals identify adherence difficulties and provide more personalized follow-up.

Growth in emerging economies
Improved diagnosis, expanding healthcare infrastructure, and increased availability of generic medicines can support treatment access across developing markets. Manufacturers that provide affordable products and strengthen local distribution may be positioned to reach additional patient populations.

Innovation in severe-asthma treatment
Advances in targeted therapies and treatment approaches for severe asthma create opportunities for pharmaceutical companies. Although biologic medicines are not necessarily inhaled treatments themselves, they form part of the broader asthma-treatment landscape and can influence the way severe disease is managed alongside inhaled therapies.

